{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Seek to negotiate an EU free movement agreement for UK citizens with EU property",
        "additional_details": "We believe it is unfair that UK citizens, who have invested into an EU country, should be restricted to accessing their property unless they pay expensive visas. UK citizens who have bought a property in an EU country have to pay tax on their property. The UK Government should seek to negotiate an agreement with the EU which ends all restrictions on the length of time UK citizens can stay in a specific EU country where they own property.",
        "background": "We want the UK Government to seek to negotiate a UK-EU freedom of movement agreement that provides UK citizens with property in the EU with unlimited free movement between the UK and the EU country they own property in. This agreement could be reciprocal for any EU nationals with property in the UK.",
